     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Block memoryDump:credentialAccess and jumpHost:lateralMovement. Blocking memoryDump stops ssoLogin and dbLogin, which in turn stops appServer, backupHost, secretsManager, vaultRead and domainAdmin. Blocking jumpHost stops mailArchive, codeRepo and serviceAccount, since jumpHost can still be reached through vpnSession or apiToken without memoryDump. That leaves all four parents of the target (mailArchive, vaultRead, dbReplica, codeRepo) unreachable. One block is not enough. Blocking only jumpHost still allows memoryDump -> ssoLogin -> appServer -> dbReplica. Blocking only memoryDump still allows jumpHost through vpnSession. Every other single block leaves the memoryDump -> jumpHost -> mailArchive path open, because memoryDump is a direct child of the footholds.\"}"
    }
